R5l wake-post implementation and prechecks
Brief18dfdb13 + service policybfd94183. Base7bb2d99e.
Scope: RT source/queue ownership plus native/offscreen/synthetic consumer drain. No protocol, ring, Cargo/lock, display frame-rate or gate budget changes.
/var/folders/zd/mv_mr2d92p5_1r8yghzbs5vw0000gn/T/rook-r5l-wake-post-hk5qcvi9

Mechanism:
Paint/model source bits remain retained through successful draw; notification admission is separate, and immediate tick/prepared sources can still wake. Queue/Latest completion clears the latch then rechecks unread data so a racing final publication or budgeted tail is rearmed. Native/offscreen raw runtime notices share one8ms deadline on the existing IO runtime; a frame can consume them earlier, and raw-only notices do not request paint.
